  "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $2$ pivots in the $1$st and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column.",
